<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss approve aviation tax deal with Saudi Arabia.</title>
<headline>Swiss approve aviation tax deal with Saudi Arabia.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss government has approved an agreement with Saudi Arabia that avoids double taxation in the area of international aviation, the foreign ministry in Berne said.</p>
<p>The deal, the product of 20 years of negotiations, frees international airlines' operational revenue from income and property taxes. It also ends taxes on mobile assets, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Swissair offices in Saudi Arabia as well as those of Saudia in Switzerland will benefit from this tax break,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
